1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """Round-80 matrix battery v7 — the subject set is drawn per run, so no digest table
3: built from committed bytes maps it (QUALITY 152 successor to round 79's limit).
4: 
5: Unit under test: a MATRIX program that takes `--counter PATH --work DIR` and exits 0
6: iff a candidate counter satisfies every case it declares. The battery runs the matrix
7: against re-emitted copies of two positives and eleven forgers (the round-76 subject
8: set, referenced byte-identically from `corpus/evidence/round76/forgers/`), three
9: forged matrices, and the two round-79 oracles that identified a subject without
10: scoring it, under the round-78 legs plus the round-78 successor requirement, and adds
11: the round-80 FRESH LEG:
12: 
13:   ORDER LEG      The subject list is permuted per run with a fresh 64-bit seed
14:                  (`secrets.randbits`). The permutation is never printed and no digest
15:                  of it is printed.
16:   QUIET LEG      No per-subject line is printed while subjects are running; every
17:                  `MATRIX RUN`/`SUBJECT` line is buffered and flushed after the scoring
18:                  loop ends.
19:   CONTENT LEG    Every matrix run must print the twelve `CASE` lines of the frozen
20:                  contract with cells equal to the battery's own independently stated
21:                  contract map, and a summary count equal to the number of `PASS` lines.
22:   IDENTITY LEG   **Re-emission, not salting.** Round 78 inserted an inert statement into
23:                  the source text, so a four-line normalizer deleted the `_r78<hex>`
24:                  family and recovered every subject byte-for-byte (`R78L1/a8-normalizer.py`).
25:                  v6 never writes the source text: it parses the subject, drops every
26:                  docstring, renames every bound identifier through a fresh per-copy table
27:                  (imports, keyword-argument names, builtins and dunders excluded), inserts
28:                  one random-named integer assignment after the last `__future__` import at a
29:                  random top-level position, compiles the tree under a random file name and
30:                  writes a wrapper that `exec`s the marshalled code object. No 40-byte window
31:                  of the committed source occurs in the copy.
32:   RECEIPT LEG    The verdict is bound to the process exit code and to a `RECEIPT_LINES`
33:                  trailer printed immediately before the predicate line.
34: 
35:   FRESH LEG      Per run the battery draws `--fresh N` fresh positives and N fresh
36:                  forgers from the two committed positives by AST rewrite (semantics-
37:                  preserving: comparison-operand swap, if/else inversion, integer
38:                  constant folding) or AST mutation (operator flip, constant shift,
39:                  condition negation, branch swap). Ground truth is MEASURED, not
40:                  assumed: the committed witness matrix (`round76/loader-matrix-v3.py`)
41:                  runs the base copy and the candidate, and the candidate is a POSITIVE
42:                  only when verdict, marks and all twelve case cells are identical;
43:                  otherwise it is a FORGER. The matrix under test must accept every
44:                  fresh positive and reject every fresh forger. The drawn set is scored
45:                  by the matrix under test AND by every enumerated oracle, so an oracle
46:                  whose table was built from committed bytes cannot reach the PASS line.
47:                  No digest table built from committed bytes maps these subjects.
48: 
49: Predicate (same sentence as `corpus/evidence/round80/claims.md`):
50: 
51:   `python3 -B corpus/evidence/round80/matrix-battery-v7.py --matrix MATRIX --work DIR
52:    --fresh 2` exits 0 and prints exactly
53:   `BATTERY=PASS forgers_rejected=11/11 positive=2/2 fresh_positive=2/2 fresh_forgers=2/2 oracles_rejected=5/5`.
54: 
55: A forger is REJECTED only when both runs exit 1 with fewer than full marks; a positive
56: is ACCEPTED only when both runs exit 0 with full marks, `MATRIX=PASS`, and a valid
57: contract table. An exit of 2 is never scored in the matrix's favour. The five
58: enumerated oracles are the three committed forged matrices, the round-79
59: structure-identity matrix and the round-79 payload-decode forger re-pointed at the
60: committed lane; each must be REJECTED.
61: 
62: Closure-removal twins (mutation evidence, never the predicate): `--no-permute` runs the
63: fixed round-76 subject order, `--no-content` drops the contract-table requirement,
64: `--print-order` re-enables the round-77 `ORDER <i> <digest>` line, and `--no-fresh`
65: drops the fresh leg (the round-79 behaviour). `--reemit-only` emits one copy of each
66: committed subject into `--work` and exits 0 (the `derivative-check.py` entry point),
67: never scoring anything.
68: 
69: Limits (recorded, not closed): the fresh leg's ground truth is the committed witness
70: matrix, so a witness that is wrong about a case makes both legs wrong together; the
71: eleven committed forgers and the five oracles are the independent anchor. A classifier
72: that knows this generator's rewrite operators can still separate fresh positives from
73: fresh forgers statically; that channel is measured by the round-80 critic seat and
74: recorded, not certified closed. Line-count detection closes append; a forger that
75: truncates the receipt is not detected by it (the caller's exit code remains
76: authoritative).
77: 
78: Usage: python3 corpus/evidence/round80/matrix-battery-v7.py --matrix PATH --work DIR
79:        [--runs N] [--matrix-timeout S] [--fresh N] [--no-fresh] [--rev REV]
80:        [--no-permute] [--no-content] [--print-order] [--reemit-only]
81: Exit: 0 BATTERY=PASS · 1 BATTERY=FAIL · 2 usage/env.
82: """
